window.OSAP_FT=window.OSAP_FT||{};window.OSAP_FT["2a"]={"https://theconversation.com/holding-the-line-how-transmission-lines-became-an-election-flashpoint-in-victoria-296502":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T16:16Z","sha":"a89388617ddc1c99d12f96333635468a8cfd0805545fe47ed2f232fc5179ac39","read":"https://theconversation.com/holding-the-line-how-transmission-lines-became-an-election-flashpoint-in-victoria-296502","bytes":190343,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Holding the line: how transmission lines became an election flashpoint in Victoria","by":[{"n":"Jonathan Pickering","r":"Associate Professor, Canberra School of Government, University of Canberra"},{"n":"Stephanie Rosestone","r":"Community Fellow, University of Canberra; Australian National University"},{"n":"Wendy Conway-Lamb","r":"Postdoctoral Research Fellow, Centre for Deliberative Democracy and Centre for Environmental Governance, University of Canberra"}],"pub":"2026-11-16T18:24:19Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["Electricity transmission lines are a ",["hot-button issue","https://www.abc.net.au/news/2026-08-19/victorian-coalition-promises-to-scrap-vni-west-transmission-line/107053638"]," in the upcoming Victorian election. Following ",["farm-gate blockades","https://www.abc.net.au/news/2026-08-06/farmers-fined-for-blocking-access-for-transmission-lines-vic/106998866"]," and protests outside the ",["Victorian parliament","https://www.abc.net.au/news/2025-08-01/transmission-line-vni-west-cost-blow-out-victoria-farmers-fight/105599880"],", both the Coalition and One Nation have ",["promised","https://www.abc.net.au/news/2026-08-20/coalition-one-nation-ripon-vni-west-election-nationals/107054552"]," to scrap a multi-billion-dollar project in the state’s northwest."]},{"k":"p","s":["If the ",["polls","https://theconversation.com/with-two-weeks-to-go-the-victorian-election-is-the-coalitions-to-lose-296248"]," are correct and Victoria changes government, what would this mean for energy policy and regional Australia?"]},{"k":"h","s":["Why are these transmission lines proposed?"]},{"k":"p","s":["For the past century, coal-fired power plants have supplied most of Victoria’s electricity. But some plants have already retired and the rest will follow. The capacity they provide urgently ",["needs replacing","https://www.abc.net.au/news/2025-05-16/coal-reliability-report-outages-loy-yang-yallourn-latrobe-valley/105296552"],". Renewables produced about ",["44%","https://www.energy.vic.gov.au/about-energy/news/news-stories/Victoria-powers-beyond-its-2025-renewable-energy-target"]," of Victoria’s electricity last year."]},{"k":"p","s":["To shift to a system largely powered by renewables, Victoria will need new high-voltage lines. These are meant to deliver energy from new rural ",["solar and wind farms","https://theenergy.co/articles/ideological-vni-west-axe-risks-12bn-in-projects"]," to cities and industrial centres, as well as stabilising the grid by making it easier to trade electricity between states."]},{"k":"p","s":["New transmission lines are a ",["key component","https://www.aemo.com.au/energy-systems/major-publications/integrated-system-plan-isp/2026-integrated-system-plan-isp"]," of ",["state","https://www.vicgrid.com.au/transmission-planning/victorian-transmission-plan"]," and ",["federal","https://www.dcceew.gov.au/energy/renewable/rewiring-the-nation"]," efforts to overhaul the National Electricity Market."]},{"k":"p","s":["In Victoria, the two biggest projects in the works are the 190-kilometre ",["Western Renewables Link","https://www.westernrenewableslink.com.au/"]," (WRL) west of Melbourne, and the Victoria to New South Wales Interconnector (VNI) West, spanning around ",["240km in Victoria","https://www.vicgrid.com.au/projects/victoria-to-nsw-interconnector-west"]," and a ",["similar length in NSW","https://www.transgrid.com.au/projects-innovation/vni-west/"],". Both are well advanced through state planning processes, but neither has begun construction."]},{"k":"p","s":["A ",["recent survey","https://www.abc.net.au/news/2026-04-30/renewable-energy-transition-support-study-australia-victoria/106615850"]," showed the energy transition has majority support in regional Victoria. But opponents of the two lines are vocal and organised."]},{"k":"h","s":["Where do the parties stand?"]},{"k":"p","s":["Vocal opponents of transmission projects are running as regional candidates for the ",["Nationals","https://www.afr.com/policy/energy-and-climate/the-power-cable-that-could-make-or-break-victoria-20261030-p6135d"]," and ",["One Nation","https://www.riverineherald.com.au/news/smith-has-runs-on-the-board/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Earlier in the election campaign, the Coalition promised to ",["pause both projects","https://www.abc.net.au/news/2026-05-07/victoria-election-coalition-vows-to-pause-transmission-projects/106651434"]," pending a review of Victoria’s transmission plan. In August, it ",["changed tack","https://www.abc.net.au/news/2026-08-20/coalition-one-nation-ripon-vni-west-election-nationals/107054552"]," on VNI West, promising to cancel it if elected."]},{"k":"p","s":["One Nation has gone further by ",["pledging to scrap","https://vic.onenation.org.au/policies/energy#power-bills"]," VNI West, WRL and other major transmission projects."]},{"k":"p","s":["In September, Premier Ben Carroll ",["ordered","https://www.abc.net.au/news/2026-09-15/western-renewables-link-ees-approval-ben-carroll-cost-assessment/107154342"]," an immediate cost assessment of WRL, but his Labor government remains committed to building VNI West."]},{"k":"p","s":["The Greens are supportive of new transmission lines to unlock renewables, but have ",["criticised","https://greens.org.au/vic/news/media-release/labor-bungles-western-renewables-link-kicks-transparency-past-election"]," the government handling of WRL."]},{"k":"h","s":["What’s driving this opposition?"]},{"k":"p","s":["Opponents ",["cite","https://www.vicgrid.com.au/__data/assets/pdf_file/0033/772449/vni-west-pacr-volume-2-additional-consultation-report-submissions.pdf"]," a range of concerns, such as disruption to farming, visual impact, bushfire risk, threats to biodiversity and pressures on local services."]},{"k":"p","s":["A ",["common theme","https://www.gannawarra.vic.gov.au/News-Media/Council-opposes-VNI-West-project"]," is that rural areas are being expected to do too much for the benefit of energy users in cities. “Our job is to feed the city not supply its electricity!”, as one ",["protest sign","https://www.abc.net.au/news/2025-08-01/transmission-line-vni-west-cost-blow-out-victoria-farmers-fight/105599880"]," put it."]},{"k":"p","s":["Most opposition doesn’t stem from a rejection of climate science, though this is a ",["feature","https://onenation.org.au/policies/climate"]," of One Nation’s policies. Experts have raised concerns about ",["misinformation and disinformation","https://www.aph.gov.au/DocumentStore.ashx?id=a1f1b6fb-f2a6-4697-8d40-f035da750faf&subId=778173"]," amplifying opposition of transmission projects. This is a factor, but there are legitimate concerns in the mix."]},{"k":"p","s":["One real point of contention is the power transmission network operators have to ",["compulsorily acquire","https://www.parliament.vic.gov.au/parliamentary-activity/hansard/hansard-details/HANSARD-2145855009-34764"]," easements on private land, allowing them access to build and maintain power lines. This is quite different to ",["solar or wind projects","https://www.theland.com.au/story/9385137/uungula-wind-farm-why-these-nsw-farmers-welcomed-69-turbines/#slide=2"]," where landholders remain free to choose whether or not to host them."]},{"k":"p","s":["The state government has ",["offered","https://www.vicgrid.com.au/__data/assets/pdf_file/0032/759533/Compensation-and-landholder-payments-factsheet.pdf"]," benefit packages of A$200,000 per kilometre to landholders hosting power lines on top of compensation payments. There are broader ",["community benefit funds","https://www.westernrenewableslink.com.au/community/benefit-sharing-program/community-fund/"],", too."]},{"k":"p","s":["Some farmers are ",["keen","https://www.abc.net.au/news/2026-04-13/farmer-for-vni-west-transmission-electricity-grid-power/106546732"]," to host transmission towers, as the stable income stream can help them through leaner years. For others, the question is less about money and more about ",["dissatisfaction","https://theconversation.com/rural-australian-communities-are-hosting-the-clean-energy-boom-are-they-getting-a-fair-say-296254"]," with the consultation process and ",["distrust","https://doi.org/10.1016/j.erss.2026.104546"]," of project backers."]},{"k":"h","s":["Flashpoints for rural discontent"]},{"k":"p","s":["For some residents, the real issue is resisting the industrialisation of rural areas, as captured in one group’s slogan: “ ",["No to lines, mines and turbines!","https://www.facebook.com/groups/554040724078738/"],"”. Others are supportive of renewables, but ",["critical","https://www.energygridalliance.com.au/critical-analysis-of-the-draft-2025-victorian-transmission-plan/"]," of proposed transmission routes."]},{"k":"p","s":["Recent ",["research","https://doi.org/10.1016/j.erss.2026.104546"]," shows opposition to transmission lines is also a proxy for bigger debates about regional Australia’s intersecting challenges, from extreme weather and cost-of-living pressures to deteriorating roads and poor access to services."]},{"k":"p","s":["The two council areas in Victoria with the highest proportion of roads in ",["poor condition","https://www.abc.net.au/news/2026-09-17/vago-report-data-dive-reveals-victoria-pothole-problem/107154372"]," (Gannawarra and Buloke) are both in VNI West’s path."]},{"k":"p","s":["Many rural residents feel their areas have ",["been forgotten","https://www.abc.net.au/news/2025-09-14/why-regional-victorians-are-angry-at-state-government/105761034"],". Saying no to transmission lines sends a message that rural communities need to be heard."]},{"k":"h","s":["Can transmission projects be done differently?"]},{"k":"p","s":["It remains to be seen whether VNI West or WRL will survive the state election. But the tensions on display in Victoria have clear lessons for future projects, as our ",["research shows","https://www.centreforenvironmentalgovernance.com/research/just-transmission%3A-advancing-coherence-in-australia%E2%80%99s-electricity-policy"],":"]},{"k":"li","s":["Early, sustained and respectful ",["community engagement","https://www.dcceew.gov.au/energy/renewable/community-engagement/transmission"]," is vital, not only on proposed transmission projects but on regional futures more broadly."]},{"k":"li","s":["People in regional Australia don’t view transmission projects in isolation, but as part of the ",["broader effects","https://reneweconomy.com.au/nsw-is-about-to-find-out-the-scale-of-cumulative-impacts-in-its-renewable-energy-zones/"]," of the clean energy transition and other stresses and uncertainties they face."]},{"k":"li","s":["Governments, businesses and communities need to ",["work together","https://theenergycharter.com.au/collaboration/bettertogether-initiatives/regional-energy-collaboration-framework/"]," at regional and local levels to manage these effects and harness ",["cumulative benefits","https://www.ngshire.vic.gov.au/files/assets/public/v/3/document-resources/council-strategies/resource-ready-final-report-16-february-2026.pdf"],", such as jobs and investment in community facilities."]},{"k":"li","s":[["Community benefit programs","https://appi.org.au/report/social-licence-and-benefit-sharing-in-the-shift-to-renewable-energy-in-regional-communities/"]," need to be ",["designed with affected communities","https://doi.org/10.1016/j.erss.2026.105027"]," rather than imposed top-down. They must be delivered as part of broader commitments by government and business to promote prosperity and wellbeing in regional communities."]},{"k":"h","s":["A people-powered energy transition"]},{"k":"p","s":["If Victoria’s transmission projects are scrapped without a credible alternative, the state will face the ",["real risk","https://theenergy.co/articles/vni-west-and-the-nem-tightrope"]," of less reliable electricity."]},{"k":"p","s":["It’s vital to keep the lights on while shifting to cheaper and cleaner sources of power. But that’s not the full picture."]},{"k":"p","s":["Rural communities have a major stake in how Australia’s energy transition pans out. It’s only fair they have a say in figuring out how the benefits to regional Australia can outweigh the costs."]}],"chars":6035},"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/bosnia-and-herzegovina":{"r":"govuk","at":"2026-11-17T16:16Z","sha":"05a7c4c30ff4cc4192f8079fcd099d338b47b7f10f9cc6f947cfb0cb8edd673a","read":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/foreign-travel-advice/bosnia-and-herzegovina","bytes":59241,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Bosnia and Herzegovina travel advice","by":[{"n":"Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","r":""}],"pub":"2013-01-09T00:00:00+00:00","mod":"2026-08-13T16:28:44+01:00","blocks":[{"k":"h","s":["Warnings and insurance"]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel disruption"]},{"k":"p","s":["The border crossing at Gradiška has been relocated to a new facility. Travellers should plan ahead and check local advice before crossing by car."]},{"k":"p","s":["The European Union’s (EU) new Entry/Exit System (EES) is now being implemented across the Schengen area. The EES may take each passenger extra time, so it is important to be prepared to wait longer than usual at EU country borders and allow more time for immigration controls if travelling to and from the Schengen area."]},{"k":"h","s":["Before you travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["No travel can be guaranteed safe. Read all the advice in this guide. You may also find it helpful to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for women travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/advice-for-women-travelling-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read our ",["guide on disability and travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/disabled-travellers"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read about ",["safety for solo and independent travel","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/solo-and-independent-travel"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["advice on volunteering and adventure travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/safer-adventure-travel-and-volunteering-overseas"]]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travel insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you choose to travel, research your destinations and ",["get appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"],". Insurance should cover your itinerary, planned activities and expenses in an emergency."]},{"k":"h","s":["About FCDO travel advice"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) provides advice about risks of travel to help you make informed decisions. Find out ",["more about FCDO travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/bosnia-and-herzegovina/email-signup"]," when this advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Travel Aware on Instagram","https://www.instagram.com/travelaware/"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["This information is for people travelling on a full ",["‘British citizen’ passport","https://www.gov.uk/types-of-british-nationality"]," from the UK. It is based on the UK government’s understanding of the current rules for the most common types of travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["The authorities in Bosnia and Herzegovina set and enforce entry rules. If you’re not sure how these requirements apply to you, contact the Bosnia and Herzegovina Embassy in the UK."]},{"k":"h","s":["Passport validity requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter Bosnia and Herzegovina, your passport must:"]},{"k":"li","s":["have a ‘date of issue’ less than 10 years before the date you arrive – if you renewed your passport before 1 October 2018, it may have a date of issue that is more than 10 years ago"]},{"k":"li","s":["have an ‘expiry date’ at least 90 days after the date you plan to leave"]},{"k":"p","s":["Check with your travel provider that your passport and other travel documents meet requirements. ",["Renew your passport","https://www.gov.uk/renew-adult-passport/renew"]," if you need to."]},{"k":"p","s":["You will be denied entry if you do not have a valid, undamaged travel document or try to use a passport that has been reported lost or stolen."]},{"k":"h","s":["Dual nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["When returning to the UK, British citizens must carry a valid ",["British passport","https://www.gov.uk/browse/abroad/passports"]," or ",["certificate of entitlement","https://www.gov.uk/right-of-abode/apply-for-a-certificate-of-entitlement"],". See ",["Dual Citizenship","https://www.gov.uk/dual-citizenship"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Visa requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can travel without a visa to Bosnia and Herzegovina for up to 90 days within a 6-month period. This applies if you travel:"]},{"k":"li","s":["as a tourist"]},{"k":"li","s":["to visit family or friends"]},{"k":"li","s":["to attend business meetings, cultural or sports events"]},{"k":"li","s":["for short-term studies or training"]},{"k":"p","s":["For all other types of travel, check the conditions for temporary residence or contact the Bosnia and Herzegovina Embassy in the UK."]},{"k":"p","s":["Make sure you get your passport stamped on entry and exit."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re a visitor, border guards will look at your entry and exit stamps to check you have not overstayed the 90-day visa-free limit. If you do not have a stamp, the Border Police may fine you when you leave."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Staying longer than 90 days in a 6-month period"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you want to stay longer than 90 days within a 6-month period, apply for a residence permit. You must provide a document showing that you have no criminal record in the UK. The British Embassy is not able to issue such a document. You can ",["get a copy of your police records","https://www.gov.uk/copy-of-police-records"]," before you travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["For more information, see the Bosnia and Herzegovina government’s page about ",["residency and work permits","https://sps.gov.ba/?page_id=2491&lang=en"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["For details about medical entry requirements and recommended vaccinations, see ",["TravelHealthPro’s Bosnia and Herzegovina guide","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/32/bosnia-and-herzegovina#Vaccine_Recommendations"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Registering your stay"]},{"k":"p","s":["All foreign nationals must register with the police within 72 hours of arrival. Hotels and some hostels will usually register their guests. If your accommodation is not arranging this, you need to ",["contact the nearest field centre (‘terenski centar’) for the Service for Foreigners’ Affairs","https://sps.gov.ba/?page_id=2545&lang=en"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travelling with children"]},{"k":"p","s":["Children aged 17 and under who are travelling unaccompanied or with an adult other than their parents, must carry a notarised letter giving permission for travel. The letter must be signed by a parent or guardian and give the name of the accompanying adult."]},{"k":"p","s":["This also applies if only one parent is accompanying the child, particularly if they have a different surname to the child’s."]},{"k":"p","s":["For further information contact the Embassy of Bosnia and Herzegovina in the UK."]},{"k":"h","s":["Customs rules"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are strict ",["rules about goods you can take into and out of Bosnia and Herzegovina","https://www.uino.gov.ba/portal/en/customs/"],". You must declare anything that may be prohibited or subject to tax or duty."]},{"k":"h","s":["Safety and security"]},{"k":"h","s":["Terrorism"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high threat of terrorist attack globally affecting UK interests and British nationals, including from groups and individuals who view the UK and British nationals as targets. Stay aware of your surroundings at all times."]},{"k":"p","s":["UK Counter Terrorism Policing has information and advice on ",["staying safe","https://www.counterterrorism.police.uk/runhidetell/"]," and what to do in the event of a terrorist attack. Find out ",["how to reduce your risk from terrorism while abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/reduce-your-risk-from-terrorism-while-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Terrorism in Bosnia and Herzegovina"]},{"k":"p","s":["Terrorist attacks in Bosnia and Herzegovina cannot be ruled out."]},{"k":"p","s":["Previous attacks have included firearms attacks on government, law enforcement interests and the public. Attacks could be indiscriminate, including in places visited by foreigners."]},{"k":"h","s":["Political situation"]},{"k":"p","s":["Public protests occur from time to time and can cause traffic disruption. Protests are normally peaceful. There is a risk of violent incidents linked to locally controversial issues, usually from the conflict of the 1990s."]},{"k":"p","s":["There has been an increase in anti-UK rhetoric from some politicians in the Republika Srpska (one of the entities that makes up the State of Bosnia and Herzegovina). This could translate into wider anti-UK sentiment. Monitor local media so you can avoid planned political demonstrations and move away if you see protestors gathering."]},{"k":"h","s":["Crime"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Protecting your belongings"]},{"k":"p","s":["Beware of pickpockets and bag-snatchers on public transport and in the tourist and pedestrian areas of Sarajevo and other cities. Make sure personal belongings, including your passport, are secure. Obvious displays of wealth, including large quantities of cash or jewellery and luxury vehicles can make you a target for opportunist thieves."]},{"k":"p","s":["There has been an increase in thefts from cars in popular tourist areas in and around Sarajevo, particularly on Mount Trebevic. Make sure your vehicle is locked and your belongings are out of sight. Take particular care in areas popular with foreign tourists and in crowded public venues."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Organised crime"]},{"k":"p","s":["Incidents of violence between organised crime groups can happen, including shootings. You are unlikely to be targeted. Remain vigilant and follow the advice of the police in the event of an incident."]},{"k":"h","s":["Old landmines and unexploded weapons"]},{"k":"p","s":["Landmines and other unexploded weapons remain from the 1992 to 1995 war. While highly populated areas and major routes are largely clear, there is still a risk in less populated and rural areas. Do not step off roads and paved areas without an experienced guide. Take care near:"]},{"k":"li","s":["the former lines of conflict"]},{"k":"li","s":["the edge of roads"]},{"k":"li","s":["the open countryside"]},{"k":"li","s":["destroyed or abandoned buildings (including in towns)"]},{"k":"li","s":["neglected land"]},{"k":"li","s":["untarred roads"]},{"k":"li","s":["woods and orchards"]},{"k":"p","s":["For further information, see ",["Mine Action Centre","https://www.bhmac.org/"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Laws and cultural differences"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Personal ID"]},{"k":"p","s":["Always carry your passport or official photo ID with you. You must be able to show some form of identification if required, including when checking into hotels. For more information, see the Ministry of Security of Bosnia and Herzegovina."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Dealing with the police"]},{"k":"p","s":["Local police do not always have English language skills and you may need the ",["services of a translator","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/translators-interpreters?country=Bosnia%20and%20Herzegovina"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Illegal drugs"]},{"k":"p","s":["Illegal drugs, including cannabis, carry severe penalties. You should expect a long jail sentence and heavy fines for possessing, using or smuggling illegal drugs, including when transiting through the airport."]},{"k":"p","s":["Airports in Bosnia and Herzegovina have excellent technology and security for detecting illegal items. This is also used to scan the baggage of transiting passengers."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Ramadan"]},{"k":"p","s":["Ramadan is a holy month for Muslims in Bosnia and Herzegovina. The dates vary by year and country."]},{"k":"p","s":["You should:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check opening hours of shops and restaurants"]},{"k":"li","s":["be aware that if hotels and restaurants are providing food or drink in fasting hours, they may separate you from other guests"]},{"k":"li","s":["follow local dress codes – clothing that does not meet local dress codes may cause more offence at this time"]},{"k":"p","s":["Get more advice when you arrive from your tour guide, hotel or business contacts."]},{"k":"hs","s":["LGBT+ travellers"]},{"k":"p","s":["Same-sex sexual activity is legal in Bosnia and Herzegovina, but LGBT+ communities continue to report incidents of discrimination and even violence. Showing affection in public is likely to be frowned upon and may receive unwelcome attention."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more ",["advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Outdoor activities and adventure tourism"]},{"k":"p","s":["Check that your travel and medical insurance cover you for any adventure activities and sports."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Diving"]},{"k":"p","s":["Diving off Mostar bridge is dangerous and has resulted in serious injuries and fatalities."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Rafting"]},{"k":"p","s":["Take care when white-water rafting in rivers or close to waterfalls. Currents can be extremely strong."]},{"k":"h","s":["Transport risks"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are planning to drive in Bosnia and Herzegovina, see ",["information on driving abroad","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad"]," and check the ",["rules of the road in the RAC’s Bosnia and Herzegovina guide","https://www.rac.co.uk/drive/travel/country/bosnia-herzegovina/"],". The guide lists driving regulations and other legal requirements you need to be aware of."]},{"k":"p","s":["Your UK driving licence is valid as long as you’re driving your own vehicle or a car hired outside of Bosnia and Herzegovina. If you’re renting or using someone else’s vehicle within the country, you must also have the ",["1968 version of the international driving permit (IDP)","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad/international-driving-permit"]," with you in the car."]},{"k":"p","s":["You cannot buy an IDP outside the UK, so get one before you travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check if you need a ",["UK sticker to drive your car outside the UK","https://www.gov.uk/displaying-number-plates/flags-identifiers-and-stickers"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re staying longer than 6 months, you will need to get a local driving licence. See ",["living in Bosnia and Herzegovina","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/living-in-bosnia-and-herzegovina"]," for more details."]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact the Bosnia and Herzegovina Embassy in the UK if you have questions about bringing a vehicle into the country. The British Embassy will not be able to help if you do not have the correct documentation."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are involved in an accident, stay at the scene and do not move your vehicle until the police arrive. Traffic police can impose on-the-spot fines for any traffic offence."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Border insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["It’s illegal to drive without at least third-party insurance. The Border Police can request printed documents to show you have it."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check your insurance is valid in Bosnia and Herzegovina. If it’s not, you can buy ‘border insurance’ at the crossings at:"]},{"k":"li","s":["Bijaca"]},{"k":"li","s":["Crveni Grm (south)"]},{"k":"li","s":["Izacici (west)"]},{"k":"li","s":["Kamensko"]},{"k":"li","s":["Karakaj and Raca (east)"]},{"k":"li","s":["Samac (north-east)"]},{"k":"li","s":["Zubci (south-east)"]},{"k":"li","s":["Doljan"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Winter equipment requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["Take care when travelling outside the main towns and cities in winter, as road conditions can worsen quickly."]},{"k":"p","s":["Between November and April you must:"]},{"k":"li","s":["have tyres with an MS, M+S or M&S mark and a stylised symbol of a snowflake – the tread should be at least 4 millimetres deep"]},{"k":"li","s":["carry snow chains and use them when road signs tell you to"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Taxis"]},{"k":"p","s":["Official taxis in Sarajevo and the major towns are well-regulated and metered. Taxi drivers from the Republika Srpska might refuse to drive to a destination in the Federation of Bosnia and Herzegovina, and the same from the Federation to the Republika Srpska."]},{"k":"p","s":["Taxi drivers at Sarajevo airport taxi rank may try to charge a ‘fixed price’ fare, rather than use a meter, or charge for luggage. Make sure you agree a price before setting off. Better deals may be available by pre-booking a taxi from an established taxi service."]},{"k":"p","s":["Do not use unlicensed taxis."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Air travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sarajevo (Butmir) International Airport is prone to fog, causing flights to be delayed or cancelled during the winter months, particularly in December and January. Many airlines will not arrange accommodation when delays are caused by bad weather. You may need to find and pay for somewhere to stay."]},{"k":"h","s":["Extreme weather and natural disasters"]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out what you can do to ",["prepare for and respond to extreme weather and natural hazards","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/tropical-cyclones"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Wildfires"]},{"k":"p","s":["Wildfires are possible in Bosnia and Herzegovina from April to October due to the dry and hot weather. Wildfires are highly dangerous and unpredictable. You should:"]},{"k":"li","s":["take care when visiting or driving through countryside"]},{"k":"li","s":["make sure cigarette ends are properly extinguished"]},{"k":"li","s":["not light fires or barbecues except in designated and marked areas"]},{"k":"li","s":["not leave any rubbish"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you see a wildfire, call the emergency services on 112. Follow any advice from the police or local authorities."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Flooding"]},{"k":"p","s":["Rainfall and snowmelt have increased the risk of flooding and landslides. Road and rail links may be affected. Check and follow advice from local authorities."]},{"k":"p","s":["Flash floods and landslides are a risk in all parts of Bosnia and Herzegovina after heavy rain. Follow instructions from local officials and traffic police."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Earthquakes"]},{"k":"p","s":["Earthquakes and small tremors are recorded throughout the year, usually without serious consequences. The US Federal Emergency Management Agency website has advice about ",["what to do before, during and after an earthquake","https://www.ready.gov/earthquakes"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Before you travel check that:"]},{"k":"li","s":["your destination can provide the healthcare you may need"]},{"k":"li","s":["you have ",["appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"]," for local treatment or unexpected medical evacuation"]},{"k":"p","s":["This is particularly important if you have a health condition or are pregnant."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency medical number"]},{"k":"p","s":["Dial 124 and ask for an ambulance."]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your insurance or medical assistance company quickly if you’re referred to a medical facility for treatment."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine recommendations and health risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["At least 8 weeks before your trip:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check the latest ",["vaccine recommendations for Bosnia and Herzegovina","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/32/bosnia-and-herzegovina#Vaccine_Recommendations"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see where to get vaccines and whether you have to pay on the ",["NHS travel vaccinations page","https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/travel-vaccinations/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["See what ",["health risks you’ll face in Bosnia and Herzegovina","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/32/bosnia-and-herzegovina"],", including biting insects and ticks."]},{"k":"p","s":["High levels of air pollution can happen across the country. See ",["air quality guidance on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/disease-details.php?dis=219"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Medication"]},{"k":"p","s":["Pharmacies may not recognise prescriptions issued in the UK. Take your prescription to a local doctor who can issue a prescription to use in Bosnia and Herzegovina."]},{"k":"p","s":["The legal status and regulation of some medicines prescribed or bought in the UK can be different in other countries."]},{"k":"p","s":[["Read best practice when travelling with medicines on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/43/medicines-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Healthcare in Bosnia and Herzegovina"]},{"k":"p","s":["Medical and dental facilities, particularly outside Sarajevo and major towns, are limited."]},{"k":"p","s":["The European Health Insurance Card (EHIC) and Global Health Insurance Card (GHIC) do not cover Bosnia and Herzegovina. Ensure that you have ",["appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"]," for local treatment or unexpected medical evacuation."]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has a list of ",["medical providers in Bosnia and Herzegovina","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/bosnia-and-herzegovina-list-of-medical-facilities/bosnia-and-herzegovina-medical-facilities"]," where some staff will speak English."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel and mental health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["FCDO guidance on travel and mental health","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-advice-for-people-with-mental-health-issues"],". There is also ",["mental health guidance on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/85/travelling-with-mental-health-conditions"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Getting help"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) cannot provide tailored advice for individual trips. Read this travel advice and carry out your own research before deciding whether to travel."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency services in Bosnia and Herzegovina"]},{"k":"p","s":["Ambulance: 124"]},{"k":"p","s":["Fire: 123"]},{"k":"p","s":["Police: 122"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contact your travel provider and insurer"]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your travel provider and your insurer if you are involved in a serious incident or emergency abroad. They will tell you if they can help and what you need to do."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Refunds and changes to travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["For refunds or changes to travel, contact your travel provider. You may also be able to make a claim through insurance. However, insurers usually require you to talk to your travel provider first."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["changing or cancelling travel plans","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice#changing-or-cancelling-travel-plans"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["where to get advice if you are in a dispute with a provider"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to access previous versions of travel advice to support a claim"]},{"k":"h","s":["Support from FCDO"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has guidance on staying safe and what to do if you need help or support abroad, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["finding English-speaking ",["lawyers","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/lawyers?country=Bosnia%20and%20Herzegovina"],", ",["funeral directors","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/funeral-directors?country=Bosnia%20and%20Herzegovina"]," and ",["translators and interpreters","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/translators-interpreters?country=Bosnia%20and%20Herzegovina"]," in Bosnia and Herzegovina"]},{"k":"li","s":["dealing with a ",["death in Bosnia and Herzegovina","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/bosnia-and-herzegovina-bereavement-information"]]},{"k":"li","s":["being ",["arrested in Bosnia and Herzegovina","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/bosnia-and-herzegovina-prisoner-pack"]]},{"k":"li","s":["getting help if you’re a ",["victim of crime","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/victim-of-crime-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["what to do if you’re ",["in hospital","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/in-hospital-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["if you’re ",["affected by a crisis","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"],", such as a terrorist attack"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contacting FCDO"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help abroad"]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["how to get help from the UK government abroad","https://www.contact.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/posts/bosnia-and-herzegovina/british-embassy-sarajevo"]," including in an emergency."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help in the UK"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can call FCDO in London if you need urgent help because something has happened to a friend or relative abroad."]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 020 7008 5000 (24 hours)"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Find out about call charges","https://www.gov.uk/call-charges"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/bosnia-and-herzegovina/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Risk information for British companies"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Overseas Business Risk service offers ",["information and advice for British companies operating in Bosnia and Herzegovina","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/overseas-business-risk-bosnia-and-herzegovina"]," on how to manage political, economic, and business security-related risks."]}],"chars":17196,"change":"New information on wait times if travelling to and from the Schengen area from Bosnia and Herzegovina. New information that the border crossing at Gradiška has been relocated to a new facility ('Warnings and insurance' page)."},"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/romania":{"r":"govuk","at":"2026-11-17T17:18Z","sha":"fb6ca15e4a815fc3b4c00732af439907eba129a48af772128afe4fb150302f98","read":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/foreign-travel-advice/romania","bytes":63583,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Romania travel advice","by":[{"n":"Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","r":""}],"pub":"2013-03-14T00:00:00+00:00","mod":"2026-09-18T14:15:40+01:00","blocks":[{"k":"h","s":["Warnings and insurance"]},{"k":"h","s":["Before you travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["No travel can be guaranteed safe. Read all the advice in this guide. You may also find it helpful to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for women travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/advice-for-women-travelling-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read our ",["guide on disability and travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/disabled-travellers"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read about ",["safety for solo and independent travel","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/solo-and-independent-travel"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["advice on volunteering and adventure travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/safer-adventure-travel-and-volunteering-overseas"]]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travel insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you choose to travel, research your destinations and ",["get appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"],". Insurance should cover your itinerary, planned activities and expenses in an emergency."]},{"k":"h","s":["About FCDO travel advice"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) provides advice about risks of travel to help you make informed decisions. Find out ",["more about FCDO travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/romania/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Travel Aware on Instagram","https://www.instagram.com/accounts/login/?next=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.instagram.com%2Ftravelaware%2F&is_from_rle"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["This information is for people travelling on a full ",["‘British citizen’ passport","https://www.gov.uk/types-of-british-nationality"]," from the UK. It is based on the UK government’s understanding of the current rules for the most common types of travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["The authorities in Romania set and enforce entry rules. If you’re not sure how these requirements apply to you, contact the ",["Romanian Embassy in the UK","https://londra.mae.ro/en/node/397"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Passport validity requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["Romania follows ",["Schengen area rules","https://europa.eu/youreurope/citizens/travel/entry-exit/non-eu-nationals/index_en.htm"],". Your passport must have:"]},{"k":"li","s":["have a ‘date of issue’ less than 10 years before the date you arrive – if you renewed your passport before 1 October 2018, it might have a date of issue that is more than 10 years ago, making it invalid for entry to the Schengen area"]},{"k":"li","s":["an ‘expiry date’ at least 3 months after the date you plan to leave the Schengen area (the expiry date does not need to be within 10 years of the date of issue)"]},{"k":"p","s":["Check with your travel provider that your passport and other travel documents meet requirements. ",["Renew your passport","https://www.gov.uk/renew-adult-passport/renew"]," if you need to."]},{"k":"p","s":["You will be denied entry if you do not have a valid travel document or try to use a passport that has been reported lost or stolen."]},{"k":"p","s":["Carry your passport if you travel from Romania to other Schengen area countries. Border guards will check it if you cross land or river borders into Bulgaria or Hungary, both are in the Schengen area."]},{"k":"p","s":["There are no routine checks when travelling by air or sea within the Schengen area, but carry your passport in case you’re asked for it."]},{"k":"h","s":["Dual nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["When returning to the UK, British citizens must carry a valid ",["British passport","https://www.gov.uk/browse/abroad/passports"]," or ",["certificate of entitlement","https://www.gov.uk/right-of-abode/apply-for-a-certificate-of-entitlement"],". See ",["Dual citizenship","https://www.gov.uk/dual-citizenship"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Visa requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can ",["travel without a visa to the Schengen area","https://www.gov.uk/travel-to-eu-schengen-area"],", which includes Romania, for up to 90 days in any 180-day period. This applies if you travel:"]},{"k":"li","s":["as a tourist"]},{"k":"li","s":["to visit family or friends"]},{"k":"li","s":["to attend business meetings, cultural or sports events"]},{"k":"li","s":["for short-term studies or training"]},{"k":"p","s":["The ",["requirements for working in Romania","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/travel-to-romania-for-work"]," are different."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re travelling to other Schengen countries as well, make sure your whole visit is within the 90-day limit. Visits to Schengen countries in the 180 days before you travel count towards your 90 days. If you overstay the 90-day visa-free limit, you may be banned from entering Schengen countries for up to 3 years."]},{"k":"p","s":["You may also need to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["show a return or onward ticket"]},{"k":"li","s":["prove that you have enough money for your stay"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Staying longer than 90 days in a 180-day period"]},{"k":"p","s":["To stay longer, check which type of visa or work permit you need with the ",["Romanian Embassy in the UK","https://londra.mae.ro/en/node/397"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re in Romania with a residence permit or long-stay visa, this does not count towards your 90-day visa-free limit."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read about ",["entry processes if you live in Romania","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/living-in-romania#passports-and-travel"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["New Schengen entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["The European Union’s (EU) new Entry/Exit System (EES) is now being implemented across the Schengen area."]},{"k":"p","s":["This means that when you travel into the Schengen area for short stays, you may need to register your biometric details, such as fingerprints and a photo. There is no cost for EES registration."]},{"k":"p","s":["On your first visit into a Schengen country, you may be asked to register your details at a special booth before proceeding to the immigration desk. Follow directions from your travel operator or the staff at your port of entry. You may also need to provide either your fingerprint or photo when you leave the Schengen area. Children aged 11 or younger will not have their fingerprints scanned but can be required to have their photo taken."]},{"k":"p","s":["You do not need to take any action before you arrive at the border on entry to the Schengen area, but EES may take each passenger extra time to complete so be prepared to wait longer than usual at the border and to allow more time for immigration controls when you depart the Schengen area. If you are departing the Schengen area by plane, allow extra time to reach your departure gate as EES checks may take place before boarding."]},{"k":"p","s":["EES is replacing the previous system of manually stamping passports when visitors arrive in the Schengen area for short stays. You may be asked to input biometric details every time you enter or exit."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you enter the Schengen area through the Port of Dover, Eurotunnel at Folkestone or Eurostar at St Pancras International, any information will be taken at the border before you leave the UK."]},{"k":"p","s":["Your digital EES record is valid for 3 years."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more ",["information on the EU Entry/Exit System and to understand which countries are in the Schengen area","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/eu-entryexit-system"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are long-term resident in a Schengen country, you are exempt from EES in all Schengen countries. The full list of EES exemptions is on ",["the EU’s official Travel Europe website.","https://travel-europe.europa.eu/en/ees/to-whom-does-ees-not-apply"]]},{"k":"p","s":["If you believe you have been incorrectly entered into EES or your record of time spent in the Schengen area is incorrect, approach border officials when you next cross the Schengen border and request a correction. If you are exempt, carry documentation confirming your status. If you believe your time spent in the Schengen area has been recorded incorrectly, raise this with border officials and be prepared to provide supporting evidence if requested."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["For details about medical entry requirements and recommended vaccinations, see ",["TravelHealthPro’s Romania guide","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/185/romania#Vaccine_Recommendations"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Customs rules"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are strict rules about ",["goods you can take into or out of Romania","https://www.customs.ro/en/"]," (in Romanian). You must declare anything that may be prohibited or subject to tax or duty."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Taking food into Romania"]},{"k":"p","s":["You cannot take ",["meat, milk or products containing them into EU countries","https://ec.europa.eu/food/animals/animalproducts/personal_imports_en"],". There are some exceptions such as powdered baby milk, baby food and special foods or pet feed required for medical reasons."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Taking money into Romania"]},{"k":"p","s":["Declare cash or travellers cheques if the value is 10,000 euros or more. You will get a certified declaration to show you brought it in with you. If you do not, your money could be seized when you leave."]},{"k":"h","s":["Leaving Romania with children aged 17 and under"]},{"k":"p","s":["To leave Romania with a child aged 17 and under who holds Romanian citizenship, you may need to show notarised parental consent if:"]},{"k":"li","s":["you are not the child’s parent"]},{"k":"li","s":["you are a parent but the other parent is not travelling with you"]},{"k":"p","s":["For more information, contact the ",["Romanian Embassy in the UK","https://londra.mae.ro/en/node/397"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["For a list of the public notaries, see the National Union of Public Notaries from Romania website."]},{"k":"h","s":["Safety and security"]},{"k":"h","s":["Terrorism"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high threat of terrorist attack globally affecting UK interests and British nationals, including from groups and individuals who view the UK and British nationals as targets. Stay aware of your surroundings at all times."]},{"k":"p","s":["UK Counter Terrorism Policing has information and advice on ",["staying safe","https://www.counterterrorism.police.uk/runhidetell/"]," and what to do in the event of a terrorist attack. Find out ",["how to reduce your risk from terrorism while abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/reduce-your-risk-from-terrorism-while-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Terrorism in Romania"]},{"k":"p","s":["Although there’s no recent history of terrorism in Romania, attacks cannot be ruled out."]},{"k":"p","s":["Attacks could be indiscriminate, including in places visited by foreign nationals."]},{"k":"h","s":["Political situation and demonstrations"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is widespread military activity in neighbouring Ukraine. See ",["Ukraine travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/ukraine"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["There have been cases of drones crossing into Romanian airspace and territorial waters, and occasionally, drones carrying explosives have landed or washed ashore in Romania. If you encounter drone activity follow guidance from local authorities, including the ",["RO-Alert mobile","https://ro-alert.ro/en/about-ro-alert-2/"]," phone alert system, and do not approach any military debris."]},{"k":"h","s":["Crime"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Protecting your belongings"]},{"k":"p","s":["Be alert to petty theft in large towns, especially Bucharest. Thieves use distraction techniques and can carry out organised attacks in groups. Take care of your passport, money and personal belongings, particularly:"]},{"k":"li","s":["near money exchanges and hotels"]},{"k":"li","s":["on public transport, especially to the airport"]},{"k":"li","s":["in main railway stations"]},{"k":"li","s":["inside airport terminals"]},{"k":"p","s":["Criminals have copied credit or debit cards in some bars and restaurants."]},{"k":"p","s":["Use a hotel safe for valuables where possible and carry a copy of your passport."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Drink spiking"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a risk of drink spiking in bars and clubs. Be careful not to take drinks from strangers or leave your drinks unattended."]},{"k":"h","s":["Laws and cultural differences"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Illegal drugs"]},{"k":"p","s":["Illegal drugs, including cannabis, carry severe penalties. You should expect a long jail sentence and heavy fines for possessing, using or smuggling illegal drugs, including when transiting through the airport."]},{"k":"p","s":["Airports in Romania have excellent technology and security for detecting illegal items. This is also used to scan the baggage of transiting passengers."]},{"k":"p","s":["Increasing numbers of people, including foreign visitors, have been arrested and received lengthy sentences for drug offences at music festivals in Romania."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Using cameras in secure areas"]},{"k":"p","s":["Most airports and military bases have signs banning photography. If you’re not sure if photography is allowed, ask permission."]},{"k":"hs","s":["LGBT+ travellers"]},{"k":"p","s":["Same-sex relationships are legal in Romania. There are active LGBT+ communities and events in Romania, though the majority of LGBT+ people are not open. Find ",["information on LGBT+ issues in Romania","https://www.mozaiqlgbt.ro/en/"]," and read more ",["advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Transport risks"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are planning to drive in Romania, see ",["information on driving abroad","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad"]," and check the ",["rules of the road in the RAC’s Romania guide","https://www.rac.co.uk/drive/travel/country/romania/"],". The guide lists driving regulations and other legal requirements you need to be aware of, such as:"]},{"k":"li","s":["carrying a first aid kit, fire extinguisher, red warning triangle and a fluorescent jacket"]},{"k":"li","s":["using winter tyres (or snow chains for certain vehicles) whenever snow, ice or sleet is on the road – common practice is for this to be between November and March"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can use a UK photocard driving licence to drive in Romania. If you still have a paper driving licence, you may need to update it to a photocard licence or get the ",["correct version of the international driving permit (IDP)","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad/international-driving-permit"]," as well."]},{"k":"p","s":["Hire car companies often have stricter requirements for their customers, such as a year of driving experience, minimum age and holding an IDP."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check if you need a ",["UK sticker to drive your car outside the UK","https://www.gov.uk/displaying-number-plates/flags-identifiers-and-stickers"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Drink-driving is a serious offence in Romania. If you are tested and found to have any alcohol in your system, you may get a fine and possible imprisonment."]},{"k":"p","s":["There is also ",["guidance on driving if you’re living in Romania","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/living-in-romania#driving-in-romania"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Driving conditions"]},{"k":"p","s":["Road conditions are variable and roads can be in a bad state of repair. Driving standards can be poor. Look out for:"]},{"k":"li","s":["double-parked cars"]},{"k":"li","s":["people suddenly braking or swerving to avoid potholes"]},{"k":"li","s":["horse-drawn carts, livestock and stray dogs in rural areas"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Accidents and vehicle damage"]},{"k":"p","s":["You must get a report at the scene of an accident in Romania. If your vehicle is damaged before you arrive in the country, ask a Romanian customs officer or police officer to write a report on the damage. Doing this will help you avoid problems when you leave Romania."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Toll roads"]},{"k":"p","s":["You must pay a ",["road toll ‘rovinieta’","https://www.roviniete.ro/en/#go-content"]," to use the national roads. Buy a vignette at border points and at most petrol stations. If you do not purchase the vignette, you may get a heavy fine."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Taxis"]},{"k":"p","s":["Most taxis in Bucharest should list prices on the side of the vehicle and display a company name. Taxi drivers sometimes overcharge foreign visitors. Taxi apps such as Uber and Bolt are generally reliable."]},{"k":"h","s":["Extreme weather and natural disasters"]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out what you can do to ",["prepare for and respond to extreme weather and natural hazards","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/tropical-cyclones"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["You may receive alerts on your mobile phone from the Romanian government in the event of extreme weather, a natural disaster or other emergency. These are in Romanian and English, and you should follow the authorities’ instructions."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Earthquakes"]},{"k":"p","s":["Romania is in a seismically active area and tremors happen regularly. The last major earthquake was in 1977. The US Federal Emergency Management Agency website has advice about ",["what to do before, during and after an earthquake","https://www.ready.gov/earthquakes"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Before you travel check that:"]},{"k":"li","s":["your destination can provide the healthcare you may need"]},{"k":"li","s":["you have ",["appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"]," for local treatment or unexpected medical evacuation"]},{"k":"p","s":["This is particularly important if you have a health condition or are pregnant."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency medical number"]},{"k":"p","s":["Dial 112 and ask for an ambulance."]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your insurance or medical assistance company quickly if you’re referred to a medical facility for treatment."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccinations and health risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["At least 8 weeks before your trip:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check latest ",["vaccine recommendations for Romania","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/185/romania#Vaccine_Recommendations"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see where to get vaccines and whether you have to pay on the ",["NHS travel vaccinations page","https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/travel-vaccinations/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["what health risks you’ll face in Romania","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/185/romania"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Altitude sickness is a risk in parts of Romania. Read more about ",["altitude sickness on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/26/altitude-illness"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Medication"]},{"k":"p","s":["The legal status and regulation of some medicines prescribed or bought in the UK can be different in other countries."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["best practice when travelling with medicines on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/43/medicines-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Healthcare in Romania"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has a ",["list of medical providers in Romania","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/medical-facilities-list-romania"]," where some staff will speak English."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Health insurance cards"]},{"k":"p","s":["To get medically necessary state healthcare in Romania, you need a Global Health Insurance Card (GHIC) or a European Health Insurance Card (EHIC)."]},{"k":"p","s":["The NHS’s ",["getting healthcare abroad webpage","https://www.nhs.uk/using-the-nhs/healthcare-abroad/apply-for-a-free-uk-global-health-insurance-card-ghic/"]," has details about:"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to apply for a GHIC"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to get temporary cover if you lose your card or it does not arrive in time"]},{"k":"li","s":["who qualifies for a new EHIC instead of a GHIC"]},{"k":"li","s":["what treatment counts as medically necessary"]},{"k":"p","s":["A GHIC or EHIC is not an alternative to travel insurance. You may have costs your GHIC or EHIC does not cover, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["changes to travel and accommodation bookings"]},{"k":"li","s":["additional standard costs for treatment"]},{"k":"li","s":["medical repatriation to the UK"]},{"k":"li","s":["treatment that is ruled non-urgent"]},{"k":"li","s":["private healthcare"]},{"k":"li","s":["private clinics"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is also ",["guidance on healthcare if you’re living in Romania","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/healthcare-in-romania"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel and mental health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["FCDO guidance on travel and mental health","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-advice-for-people-with-mental-health-issues"],". There is also ",["mental health guidance on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/85/travelling-with-mental-health-conditions"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Getting help"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) cannot provide tailored advice for individual trips. Read this travel advice and carry out your own research before deciding whether to travel."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency services in Romania"]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 112 (ambulance, fire, police)"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contact your travel provider and insurer"]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your travel provider and your insurer if you are involved in a serious incident or emergency abroad. They will tell you if they can help and what you need to do."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Refunds and changes to travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["For refunds or changes to travel, contact your travel provider. You may also be able to make a claim through insurance. However, insurers usually require you to talk to your travel provider first."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["changing or cancelling travel plans","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice#changing-or-cancelling-travel-plans"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["where to get advice if you are in a dispute with a provider"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to access previous versions of travel advice to support a claim"]},{"k":"h","s":["Support from FCDO"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has guidance on staying safe and what to do if you need help or support abroad, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["finding English-speaking ",["lawyers","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/lawyers?country=Romania"],", ",["funeral directors","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/funeral-directors?country=Romania"]," and ",["translators and interpreters","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/translators-interpreters?country=Romania"]," in Romania"]},{"k":"li","s":["dealing with a ",["death in Romania","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/what-to-do-after-a-british-person-dies-in-romania"]]},{"k":"li","s":["being ",["arrested in Romania","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/romania-prisoner-pack"]]},{"k":"li","s":["getting help if you’re a ",["victim of crime","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/victim-of-crime-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["what to do if you’re ",["in hospital","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/in-hospital-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["if you’re ",["affected by a crisis","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"],", such as a terrorist attack"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contacting FCDO"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help abroad"]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["how to get help from the UK government abroad","https://www.contact.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/posts/romania/british-embassy-bucharest"]," including in an emergency."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help in the UK"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can call FCDO in London if you need urgent help because something has happened to a friend or relative abroad."]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 020 7008 5000 (24 hours)"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Find out about call charges","https://www.gov.uk/call-charges"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/romania/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Risk information for British companies"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Overseas Business Risk service offers ",["information and advice for British companies operating in Romania","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/overseas-business-risk-romania"]," on how to manage political, economic, and business security-related risks."]}],"chars":16581,"change":"New information about drones crossing into Romanian airspace (‘Safety and security’ page)."},"https://theconversation.com/has-chalmers-really-made-180-billion-in-budget-savings-it-depends-where-you-start-from-296479":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T20:06Z","sha":"73a7412ed72e996f3602304541ff6275b8ddef7749f574c13b16d8ac67f1ca98","read":"https://theconversation.com/has-chalmers-really-made-180-billion-in-budget-savings-it-depends-where-you-start-from-296479","bytes":179722,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Has Chalmers really made $180 billion in budget savings? It depends where you start from","by":[{"n":"Stephen Bartos","r":"Professor of Economics, University of Canberra"}],"pub":"2026-11-17T19:08:25Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["The federal government claims to have delivered A$180 billion of savings since it came to office. The figure was ",["put out","https://ministers.pmc.gov.au/gallagher/responsible-economic-and-fiscal-management"]," at the time of the May budget, and has been repeated frequently by Treasurer Jim Chalmers since then."]},{"k":"p","s":["It’s probably accurate – it would have been verified by Finance and Treasury officials before it was published – but it does not tell the whole story. Federal government spending has now reached its highest level since the COVID pandemic. If the government has saved $180 billion, why is total spending going up?"]},{"k":"p","s":["The answer is that the $180 billion figure is gross, not net – that is, while savings have been made in some areas, the government has increased spending elsewhere."]},{"k":"h","s":["The budget bottom line"]},{"k":"p","s":["Economist Chris Richardson in a social media ",["post","https://x.com/ChrisEconomist"]," noted the “cumulative cost to the budget of government decisions since first elected has been $103 billion […] Decisions have made the budget worse, not better”."]},{"k":"p","s":["His figure, derived from the official budget papers, is net. That is, new spending decisions have more than outweighed savings made elsewhere. It’s a bit like spending $20 less on groceries at the supermarket, but then picking up takeaway for $30 on the way home."]},{"k":"p","s":["Nevertheless, without the government’s gross savings, the bottom line would be $180 billion further in deficit. Whether spending growth makes a budget “worse” is a value judgement. Many people highly value ",["the services provided","https://theconversation.com/are-australians-really-overtaxed-it-depends-what-you-think-government-should-do-293113"]," through government spending."]},{"k":"p","s":["Moreover, the economic impact depends on circumstances. In a recession, governments should spend more, to stimulate the economy."]},{"k":"p","s":["Right now, however, we are not in a recession. The economy is ",["growing","https://theconversation.com/australias-economy-grows-by-2-1-but-peoples-living-standards-arent-keeping-pace-290822"],", albeit slowly."]},{"k":"p","s":["Inflation is higher than the Reserve Bank would like, which has led the RBA to hike interest rates five times this year. There are questions – explored ",["elsewhere","https://theconversation.com/inflation-is-proving-more-stubborn-in-australia-than-elsewhere-making-the-rbas-job-harder-295878"]," in The Conversation – about what is causing inflation. There are differences over whether interest rates are the best tool, and what government should do."]},{"k":"p","s":["RBA Assistant Governor Sarah Hunter in a recent ",["interview","https://www.rba.gov.au/speeches/2026/sp-ag-2026-10-25.html"]," confirmed the RBA’s view that government spending was contributing to demand – that is, contributing to inflation."]},{"k":"h","s":["Mid-year review is coming"]},{"k":"p","s":["Finance Minister Katy Gallagher has ",["foreshadowed","https://www.canberratimes.com.au/story/9385345/katy-gallagher-flags-aps-savings-in-myefo-after-rba-rate-hike/"]," savings will be announced in the Mid-year Fiscal and Economic Outlook (MYEFO) in December. But some ",["reports","https://www.abc.net.au/news/2026-11-01/katy-gallagher-wont-promise-myefo-net-savings/107333248"]," suggest these may not be net savings – that is, they will be offset by other spending."]},{"k":"p","s":["The picture is complicated by methodology. The baseline against which savings are measured is the forward estimates, the official estimates for planned spending over the next four years. This means the government can claim a saving, even if spending goes up, if policy decisions lead to spending growing at a slower pace than originally estimated."]},{"k":"p","s":["A good illustration of this is the National Disability Insurance Scheme (NDIS). In the last budget, the government ",["promised","https://budget.gov.au/content/05-care-and-opportunity.htm"]," NDIS savings of $37.8 billion over the next four years, mainly through tighter eligibility and reduced support packages."]},{"k":"p","s":["That has not stopped the NDIS growing – the savings made have merely ",["slowed the rate of growth","https://www.aph.gov.au/About_Parliament/Parliamentary_departments/Parliamentary_Library/Research/Research_Note/2026-27/NDISExpenditureProjections"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["At the same time it is trying to achieve savings through policy decisions, other spending often rises for reasons beyond the government’s control."]},{"k":"p","s":["It could be health sector costs, rising interest payments on government debt, numbers of people eligible for pensions and benefits, or the ",["blowout in the Snowy Hydro","https://theconversation.com/why-snowy-hydros-25-billion-cost-blowout-is-a-warning-sign-for-other-megaprojects-295057"]," 2.0 scheme. These cost increases undermine any savings target a government might set to help fight inflation."]},{"k":"p","s":["On Tuesday, Chalmers ",["told a conference","https://www.abc.net.au/news/2026-11-17/chalmers-says-mid-year-budget-update-to-contain-cuts/107393416"]," the government is aiming to “cut enough, but not too much” in the MYEFO. “It will strike some fine balances,” he said."]},{"k":"h","s":["Little trims to spending aren’t enough"]},{"k":"p","s":["To make any difference to inflation the government has to reduce spending significantly – not take small shavings around the edges. This means looking at the big areas of government spending: social security and welfare, health, defence and GST payments to the states."]},{"k":"p","s":["Savings in these areas are difficult and most of the obvious areas have already been ruled out."]},{"k":"p","s":["Even if many commentators would like the government to scrap its commitment to nuclear-powered submarines under the AUKUS deal, the government (with Opposition support) remains committed to them."]},{"k":"p","s":["Even if the Productivity Commission and most economists including ",["Saul Eslake","https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2026/nov/10/what-would-tip-australian-economy-into-recession"]," would like the government to save money by ending the special deal with Western Australia on the carve-up of the GST, the government has ",["already said no","https://theconversation.com/the-controversial-gst-deal-with-the-states-is-under-review-there-are-better-alternatives-266054"],". Maybe it will reconsider at MYEFO."]},{"k":"p","s":["Modest proposed savings, such as removing the ",["extra private health rebate","https://theconversation.com/exempting-pensioners-from-private-health-rebate-changes-wont-make-it-fairer-heres-what-would-294945"]," paid to pensioners, get knocked back by the parliament for political reasons."]},{"k":"p","s":["Similarly, cuts to health, aged pensions, or payments to the states for hospitals and education, are likely to be off the table because of the risk of political backlash."]},{"k":"p","s":["This leaves the government with a smaller menu of programs where it could make savings."]},{"k":"p","s":["It still has plenty of options. It could:"]},{"k":"li","s":["trawl the backwaters of government to find outdated programs to cut"]},{"k":"li","s":["abolish numerous discretionary grants and handouts"]},{"k":"li","s":["reintroduce wider means testing."]},{"k":"p","s":["All are helpful to the budget bottom line, even if they won’t ",["solve the inflation problem","https://www.news24.com.au/politics/australian-politics/labor-warns-there-is-no-level-of-savings-that-will-make-inflation-disappear-as-jim-chalmers-faces-pressure-to-rein-in-spending/news-story/fc1e47d021e26ffe8134ce826eb71dec"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["The Opposition has put forward ",["its own plan","https://www.liberal.org.au/2026/10/26/coalition-will-cut-labors-waste-cut-taxes-and-tackle-the-cost-of-living"]," to save $31 billion, starting in 2028-29."]},{"k":"p","s":["The largest component is cuts to energy transition programs, including abolishing the Net Zero Economy Agency. As with the savings likely to be announced at MYEFO, they are genuine cuts which would make some difference – but spread over four years, not enough to shift the dial on inflation."]}],"chars":5609}};
